do what we need to do to protect our  civilian population as i believe the  british government would do to protect  the british  population and of course our goal is to  bring about  long-term peace and quiet we want to see  a situation  where israeli civilians don't have to  live in fear of an incoming rocket sent  by gaza  we've had now three nights in a row  where the sirens have been going off in  major population centers in israel where  people are being running to the bomb  shelters my family included  this is a a difficult time but there's  no point  as i said before to have some sort of a  band-aid quick fix only to go through  all this again next week  we want to come out of this with a  sustained period of quiet  we want to we want a new reality where  we don't have to live fear in fear of  these incoming rockets  i think i mean you talk about the  importance of safety for civilians  everybody understands that but what  about palestinian civilians we  know we think 65 people in gaza have  died how many of those were civilians we  don't know apart from the number  that there are at least 14 palestinian  children who've died  i mean a lot of people are looking at  this and saying you know although they  understand  the need for israel to defend itself  this is  not a proportional response  well i want you to say i want to say  first off that we don't want to see  anyone  uh innocent people caught up in the  crossfire between us and hamas  we don't want to see anyone hurt  unnecessarily and of course  heaven forbid children that's the last  thing we want to see i mean every time  a child is killed israeli or palestinian  it's a tragedy  it shouldn't happen but we face a very  difficult dilemma here  because hamas is actually committing a  double war crime they are not only  indiscriminately shooting at israeli  civilians  bombarding our cities with volley after  volley after of rocket but at the same  time they implant their terrorist  military machine  inside civilian neighborhoods they fire  from mosques from school  from schools to built up areas and if we  want to take out their rocket launchers  we have to try to be as surgically as is  possible  in in in a very very complex combat  situation  often with civilians in the vicinity now  we try to be as surgical as we can we  don't want to hit the civilians  but hamas in doing so is committing a  second war crime not only are they  attacking israeli civilians but they're  deliberately exploiting and abusing the  gaza civilian population  as a human shield for their military  terrorist machine  i mean you you talk about them  committing war crimes one  of uh of our mps over here who  who has a palestinian mum as it goes but  she's been  looking at the situation in sheikh  jarrah and saying  well that in itself from the actions  that israel is taking is  is breaking the fourth geneva convention  i i i beg to disagree what you have in  sheikh is is a land dispute between  between two different groups two  different uh individuals  where you have property there were jews  living in czech church before the 1948  war  and they now claim that they want to  return to that property now the israeli  government hasn't taken a side in the  court case  but this is a land dispute but surely we  can all agree that in any land dispute  there does not have to be violence there  definitely doesn't have to be an excuse  for people to send missiles into israel  but in terms of stepping back from the  brink here which the international  community  is really calling for really trying to  apply pressure  on both sides here to do that wouldn't  stopping this  whatever is going on in shake gerard at  the moment putting a pause on that  trying to take a step back trying to get  behind the negotiating table again  be a really important move at this stage  i think it's important to remember that  the problem here is hamas  the palestinian government is someone  we've negotiated with in the past 